# Backend Architecture

- Keep `apps/backend` as a modular monolith unless an ADR says otherwise.
- Put business logic in backend modules, not in the frontend.
- Use Prisma as the data access layer and `schema.prisma` as the database source of truth.
- Preserve soft multi-tenancy patterns such as `organization_id` on tenant-owned data.
- Prefer additive changes over speculative abstractions.
- If backend boundaries materially change, update `docs/architecture/current.md` and consider an ADR.
